  "dataNotes": "Olympic is private and publishes no scorecard. Hole pars (member par 71), Championship-tee yards, men's stroke indexes, and men's ratings/slopes come from the USGA-derived card on Stymie, which includes the 7,214-yd Championship tee added in the 2023 Hanse/Wagner renovation. Greenskeeper's card has the same Black/Blue/White yardages and ratings, but its stroke indexes for holes 4 and 6 are swapped (3 and 7) and it lacks the Championship tee, so it looks older; Stymie's indexes were used. The 2012 U.S. Open was played at par 70, with hole 1 as a long par 4; members play it as a par 5 (par 71). The USGA NCRDB blocked automated access. All photos predate the 2023 renovation (2012 U.S. Open week and earlier). The holes have no names.",
